  "manual_cleanup": "Only the 64 baseline leftover private partials were manually removed after their normal-GC sizes were recorded. Not counted as reclaimed files; the complete experiment root and venvs were removed only after all remote calls completed.",
  "probe_sources_sha256": {
    "incomplete_publication_probe.py": "bf1a6f621d71ad77a4217c22439be403a68cfa2e230966e293cad3a44b0ac78b",
    "incomplete_cleanup_fault.c": "054096447bb772d6398d464d643a48e87d46124c3d99ca3cab32f889fefaef60"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Accurate offset capture, exclusive stable file identity, PID guard placement, descriptor handoff, syscall dispatch and catalog retirement are not mechanically refined to the model. Verus proves actual generic controller functions and PID equality, not the complete I/O adapter.",
    "Prefix length invariants do not prove byte preservation; EnvironmentIncomplete supplies the truncate prefix-preservation contract. Failed syscalls may already take effect; successful durability and truthful unlink absence remain environmental contracts.",
    "Storage-crash actions retain a live client descriptor, not writer-process restart. Failures before successful open/packed seek, process death and abandoned internal holds can still leak safely; historical leftovers are not automatically repaired or scanned.",
    "No automatic background cleanup retry, orphan sweep, timeout-based writer seal or TTL fencing is introduced. Completion requires a live caller to retry.",
    "Four hosts independently execute same-host live-writer retry on the shared filesystem. New syscall errors are injected before/after actual calls, not natural deployment faults, cross-host writer recovery or power-loss certification.",
    "All hosts report filesystem type fuseblk; this is not a JuiceFS version/configuration attestation. Logical namespace byte removal does not certify immediate physical capacity reclamation.",
    "Timing groups are small (n=8 failure, n=4 retry); nearest-rank p99 equals maximum. Caches/background load uncontrolled. Failure latency includes extra safety barriers and is not a bandwidth comparison.",
    "Sparse roughly-2-TiB offsets are not physical TB transfer. This final binary has no new 100 GB throughput result; prior 100 GB evidence retains its own binary identity.",
    "Finite model checks and selected actual Rust proofs do not establish that all bugs are absent."
  ],
